{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You want a table that fills while the model writes JSON. If you wait for the full object, the UI stays empty."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stream: true"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":". Pass the same schema to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":". Show "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"partial.rows"},{"type":"text","value":" as table rows."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This tutorial is React + Start. For other frameworks, open "},{"type":"link","href":"../getting-started/quick-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quick Start"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can skip the scaffold and paste a key in the sandbox at the end of this page."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you already built "},{"type":"link","href":"./basic-chat","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic Chat"}]},{"type":"text","value":", keep the key form. Then skip to the schema."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"1-create-a-start-app","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Create a Start app"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npx @tanstack/cli@latest create","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pick React. For more options, see "},{"type":"link","href":"https://tanstack.com/start/latest/docs/framework/react/quick-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Start getting started"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Then install the TanStack AI packages and Zod:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-react\",\"@tanstack/ai-openrouter\",\"zod\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Get an OpenRouter key from "},{"type":"link","href":"https://openrouter.ai","children":[{"type":"text","value":"openrouter.ai"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"client-and-server","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client and server"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A structured table has two sides."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"client"}]},{"type":"text","value":" holds the key, sends the prompt, and shows rows from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"partial"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"server"}]},{"type":"text","value":" route reads that key, calls OpenRouter with the schema, and streams JSON back."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The next steps share one schema. Then they save the key. Then they show the table. Then they add the route."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"2-share-a-schema","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Share a schema"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/lib/table-schema.ts"},{"type":"text","value":". The client and the server import this file. Field descriptions tell the model what to put in each column."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { z } from 'zod'\n\nexport const tableSchema = z.object({\n  title: z.string().meta({ description: 'Short title for the table' }),\n  rows: z.array(\n    z.object({\n      name: z.string().meta({ description: 'Row name' }),\n      year: z.number().meta({ description: 'First release year' }),\n      kind: z.string().meta({ description: 'Category or paradigm' }),\n      note: z.string().meta({ description: 'One-line typical use' }),\n    }),\n  ),\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"3-set-up-byok-on-the-client","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Set up BYOK on the client"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/lib/byok.ts"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryStorage()"},{"type":"text","value":" keeps the key in this tab."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineByok, memoryStorage } from '@tanstack/ai-react/byok'\nimport { openrouterByok } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok'\n\nexport const byok = defineByok({\n  storage: memoryStorage(),\n  providers: [openrouterByok],\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/components/open-router-key-form.tsx"},{"type":"text","value":". Export "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OpenRouterKeyForm"},{"type":"text","value":" from that file. If you already have this form from Basic Chat, reuse it."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useState } from 'react'\nimport { openrouterByok } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok'\nimport { useByok } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { byok } from '@/lib/byok'\n\nexport function OpenRouterKeyForm() {\n  const snapshot = useByok(byok)\n  const [draft, setDraft] = useState('')\n  const [error, setError] = useState('')\n  const status = snapshot.status[openrouterByok.id]\n  const masked = status && 'masked' in status ? status.masked : undefined\n  const missingKey = snapshot.prompt?.reason === 'missing'\n\n  return (\n    <form\n      onSubmit={(event) => {\n        event.preventDefault()\n        const next = draft.trim()\n        if (!next) return\n        setError('')\n        void byok\n          .update(openrouterByok.id, next)\n          .then(() => setDraft(''))\n          .catch((caught: unknown) =>\n            setError(\n              caught instanceof Error ? caught.message : 'Could not save key',\n            ),\n          )\n      }}\n    >\n      <input\n        type=\"password\"\n        autoComplete=\"off\"\n        placeholder={masked ? `Saved ${masked}` : 'Paste your OpenRouter key'}\n        value={draft}\n        onChange={(event) => setDraft(event.target.value)}\n      />\n      <button type=\"submit\" disabled={!draft.trim()}>\n        Save key\n      </button>\n      {missingKey ? (\n        <p>Paste an OpenRouter key, then send again.</p>\n      ) : null}\n      {error ? <p>{error}</p> : null}\n    </form>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you want passkeys, open "},{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/byok","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bring Your Own Key"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"4-show-the-table-from-partial","children":[{"type":"text","value":"4. Show the table from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"partial"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Open "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/routes/index.tsx"},{"type":"text","value":". Import "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OpenRouterKeyForm"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@/components/open-router-key-form"},{"type":"text","value":". Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"byok"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema: tableSchema"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server streams JSON text in chunks. The hook parses that incomplete JSON into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"partial"},{"type":"text","value":". Fields show up as soon as they parse. A new row can have empty cells until more text arrives."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"final"},{"type":"text","value":" is the completed object. It stays "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" until the stream ends. If you only read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"final"},{"type":"text","value":", the table stays empty until the run is done."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Show "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"partial.rows"},{"type":"text","value":" while the model writes. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"final"},{"type":"text","value":" when you need the complete object, for example to save it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Missing cells show "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"…"},{"type":"text","value":" until that field arrives."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useState } from 'react'\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents, useChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { OpenRouterKeyForm } from '@/components/open-router-key-form'\nimport { byok } from '@/lib/byok'\nimport { tableSchema } from '@/lib/table-schema'\n\nfunction TablePage() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState('')\n  const { sendMessage, isLoading, error, stop, partial, final } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    byok,\n    outputSchema: tableSchema,\n  })\n\n  const rows = partial.rows ?? []\n  const title = partial.title\n\n  const handleSendMessage = () => {\n    if (!input.trim()) return\n    sendMessage(input.trim())\n    setInput('')\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>Streaming structured table</h1>\n      <OpenRouterKeyForm />\n      {rows.length === 0 && !isLoading ? (\n        <p>Paste an OpenRouter key. Then ask for a comparison table.</p>\n      ) : (\n        <table aria-busy={isLoading}>\n          <caption>\n            {title ?? 'Results'}\n            {isLoading ? ' (streaming)' : final ? ' (complete)' : ''}\n          </caption>\n          <thead>\n            <tr>\n              <th scope=\"col\">Name</th>\n              <th scope=\"col\">Year</th>\n              <th scope=\"col\">Kind</th>\n              <th scope=\"col\">Note</th>\n            </tr>\n          </thead>\n          <tbody>\n            {rows.map((row, index) => (\n              <tr key={index}>\n                <th scope=\"row\">{row.name ?? '…'}</th>\n                <td>{row.year ?? '…'}</td>\n                <td>{row.kind ?? '…'}</td>\n                <td>{row.note ?? '…'}</td>\n              </tr>\n            ))}\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n      )}\n      {error ? <p>{error.message}</p> : null}\n      {isLoading ? (\n        <button type=\"button\" onClick={stop}>\n          Stop\n        </button>\n      ) : null}\n      <label htmlFor=\"table-prompt\">Prompt</label>\n      <textarea\n        id=\"table-prompt\"\n        value={input}\n        onChange={(event) => setInput(event.target.value)}\n        placeholder=\"Compare 6 JavaScript frameworks\"\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      />\n      <button\n        type=\"button\"\n        onClick={handleSendMessage}\n        disabled={!input.trim() || isLoading}\n      >\n        Send\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/')({\n  component: TablePage,\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A send with no key does not POST. The form shows \"Paste an OpenRouter key, then send again.\""}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"5-add-the-server-route","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5. Add the server route"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/routes/api.chat.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/routes"},{"type":"text","value":" folder, next to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"index.tsx"},{"type":"text","value":". Start maps that file name to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/api/chat"},{"type":"text","value":" path."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getByokKey"},{"type":"text","value":" reads the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x-byok-openrouter"},{"type":"text","value":" header, then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OPENROUTER_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" in the environment. If both are empty, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"byokMissing"},{"type":"text","value":" returns HTTP 401."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema: tableSchema"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stream: true"},{"type":"text","value":". Wrap "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toServerSentEventsResponse"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createOpenRouterText } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter'\nimport { openrouterByok } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok'\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from '@tanstack/ai/byok/server'\nimport { tableSchema } from '@/lib/table-schema'\n\nexport async function POST({ request }: { request: Request }) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, openrouterByok)\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(openrouterByok)\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: createOpenRouterText('openai/gpt-5.5', apiKey),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    threadId: params.threadId,\n    runId: params.runId,\n    outputSchema: tableSchema,\n    stream: true,\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/chat')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST,\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openrouterByok"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok"},{"type":"text","value":", not from the adapter main entry."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run the app. Paste an OpenRouter key. Send "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Compare 6 JavaScript frameworks"},{"type":"text","value":". Rows appear as the JSON streams."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same app is on the Examples tab at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/ai/latest/docs/framework/react/examples/streaming-structured-table"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"component","name":"client-example","attributes":{"library":"ai","framework":"react","slug":"streaming-structured-table"},"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You have a table that fills from streamed structured output. The OpenRouter key never sits in a server env file."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The full example is on GitHub: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/react/streaming-structured-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack/ai "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/react/streaming-structured-table"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For the API details, open "},{"type":"link","href":"../structured-outputs/streaming","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streaming UIs"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"1-create-a-start-app","text":"1. Create a Start app","level":2},{"id":"client-and-server","text":"Client and server","level":2},{"id":"2-share-a-schema","text":"2. Share a schema","level":2},{"id":"3-set-up-byok-on-the-client","text":"3. Set up BYOK on the client","level":2},{"id":"4-show-the-table-from-partial","text":"4. Show the table from partial","level":2},{"id":"5-add-the-server-route","text":"5. Add the server route","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou want a table that fills while the model writes JSON. If you wait for the full object, the UI stays empty.\n\nPass `outputSchema` and `stream: true` to `chat()`. Pass the same schema to `useChat`. Show `partial.rows` as table rows.\n\nThis tutorial is React + Start. For other frameworks, open [Quick Start](../getting-started/quick-start).\n\nYou can skip the scaffold and paste a key in the sandbox at the end of this page.\n\nIf you already built [Basic Chat](./basic-chat), keep the key form. Then skip to the schema.\n\n## 1. Create a Start app\n\n```bash\nnpx @tanstack/cli@latest create\n```\n\nPick React. For more options, see [Start getting started](https://tanstack.com/start/latest/docs/framework/react/quick-start).\n\nThen install the TanStack AI packages and Zod:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-react @tanstack/ai-openrouter zod\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nGet an OpenRouter key from [openrouter.ai](https://openrouter.ai).\n\n## Client and server\n\nA structured table has two sides.\n\nThe **client** holds the key, sends the prompt, and shows rows from `partial`.\n\nThe **server** route reads that key, calls OpenRouter with the schema, and streams JSON back.\n\nThe next steps share one schema. Then they save the key. Then they show the table. Then they add the route.\n\n## 2. Share a schema\n\nCreate `src/lib/table-schema.ts`. The client and the server import this file. Field descriptions tell the model what to put in each column.\n\n```typescript\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nexport const tableSchema = z.object({\n  title: z.string().meta({ description: 'Short title for the table' }),\n  rows: z.array(\n    z.object({\n      name: z.string().meta({ description: 'Row name' }),\n      year: z.number().meta({ description: 'First release year' }),\n      kind: z.string().meta({ description: 'Category or paradigm' }),\n      note: z.string().meta({ description: 'One-line typical use' }),\n    }),\n  ),\n})\n```\n\n## 3. Set up BYOK on the client\n\nCreate `src/lib/byok.ts`. `memoryStorage()` keeps the key in this tab.\n\n```typescript\nimport { defineByok, memoryStorage } from '@tanstack/ai-react/byok'\nimport { openrouterByok } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok'\n\nexport const byok = defineByok({\n  storage: memoryStorage(),\n  providers: [openrouterByok],\n})\n```\n\nCreate `src/components/open-router-key-form.tsx`. Export `OpenRouterKeyForm` from that file. If you already have this form from Basic Chat, reuse it.\n\n```tsx ignore\nimport { useState } from 'react'\nimport { openrouterByok } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok'\nimport { useByok } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { byok } from '@/lib/byok'\n\nexport function OpenRouterKeyForm() {\n  const snapshot = useByok(byok)\n  const [draft, setDraft] = useState('')\n  const [error, setError] = useState('')\n  const status = snapshot.status[openrouterByok.id]\n  const masked = status && 'masked' in status ? status.masked : undefined\n  const missingKey = snapshot.prompt?.reason === 'missing'\n\n  return (\n    <form\n      onSubmit={(event) => {\n        event.preventDefault()\n        const next = draft.trim()\n        if (!next) return\n        setError('')\n        void byok\n          .update(openrouterByok.id, next)\n          .then(() => setDraft(''))\n          .catch((caught: unknown) =>\n            setError(\n              caught instanceof Error ? caught.message : 'Could not save key',\n            ),\n          )\n      }}\n    >\n      <input\n        type=\"password\"\n        autoComplete=\"off\"\n        placeholder={masked ? `Saved ${masked}` : 'Paste your OpenRouter key'}\n        value={draft}\n        onChange={(event) => setDraft(event.target.value)}\n      />\n      <button type=\"submit\" disabled={!draft.trim()}>\n        Save key\n      </button>\n      {missingKey ? (\n        <p>Paste an OpenRouter key, then send again.</p>\n      ) : null}\n      {error ? <p>{error}</p> : null}\n    </form>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nIf you want passkeys, open [Bring Your Own Key](../advanced/byok).\n\n## 4. Show the table from `partial`\n\nOpen `src/routes/index.tsx`. Import `OpenRouterKeyForm` from `@/components/open-router-key-form`. Pass `byok` and `outputSchema: tableSchema` to `useChat`.\n\nThe server streams JSON text in chunks. The hook parses that incomplete JSON into `partial`. Fields show up as soon as they parse. A new row can have empty cells until more text arrives.\n\n`final` is the completed object. It stays `null` until the stream ends. If you only read `final`, the table stays empty until the run is done.\n\nShow `partial.rows` while the model writes. Use `final` when you need the complete object, for example to save it.\n\nMissing cells show `…` until that field arrives.\n\n```tsx ignore\nimport { useState } from 'react'\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents, useChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { OpenRouterKeyForm } from '@/components/open-router-key-form'\nimport { byok } from '@/lib/byok'\nimport { tableSchema } from '@/lib/table-schema'\n\nfunction TablePage() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState('')\n  const { sendMessage, isLoading, error, stop, partial, final } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    byok,\n    outputSchema: tableSchema,\n  })\n\n  const rows = partial.rows ?? []\n  const title = partial.title\n\n  const handleSendMessage = () => {\n    if (!input.trim()) return\n    sendMessage(input.trim())\n    setInput('')\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>Streaming structured table</h1>\n      <OpenRouterKeyForm />\n      {rows.length === 0 && !isLoading ? (\n        <p>Paste an OpenRouter key. Then ask for a comparison table.</p>\n      ) : (\n        <table aria-busy={isLoading}>\n          <caption>\n            {title ?? 'Results'}\n            {isLoading ? ' (streaming)' : final ? ' (complete)' : ''}\n          </caption>\n          <thead>\n            <tr>\n              <th scope=\"col\">Name</th>\n              <th scope=\"col\">Year</th>\n              <th scope=\"col\">Kind</th>\n              <th scope=\"col\">Note</th>\n            </tr>\n          </thead>\n          <tbody>\n            {rows.map((row, index) => (\n              <tr key={index}>\n                <th scope=\"row\">{row.name ?? '…'}</th>\n                <td>{row.year ?? '…'}</td>\n                <td>{row.kind ?? '…'}</td>\n                <td>{row.note ?? '…'}</td>\n              </tr>\n            ))}\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n      )}\n      {error ? <p>{error.message}</p> : null}\n      {isLoading ? (\n        <button type=\"button\" onClick={stop}>\n          Stop\n        </button>\n      ) : null}\n      <label htmlFor=\"table-prompt\">Prompt</label>\n      <textarea\n        id=\"table-prompt\"\n        value={input}\n        onChange={(event) => setInput(event.target.value)}\n        placeholder=\"Compare 6 JavaScript frameworks\"\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      />\n      <button\n        type=\"button\"\n        onClick={handleSendMessage}\n        disabled={!input.trim() || isLoading}\n      >\n        Send\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/')({\n  component: TablePage,\n})\n```\n\nA send with no key does not POST. The form shows \"Paste an OpenRouter key, then send again.\"\n\n## 5. Add the server route\n\nCreate `src/routes/api.chat.ts` in the `src/routes` folder, next to `index.tsx`. Start maps that file name to the `/api/chat` path.\n\n`getByokKey` reads the `x-byok-openrouter` header, then `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` in the environment. If both are empty, `byokMissing` returns HTTP 401.\n\nPass `outputSchema: tableSchema` and `stream: true`. Wrap `chat()` with `toServerSentEventsResponse`.\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createOpenRouterText } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter'\nimport { openrouterByok } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok'\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from '@tanstack/ai/byok/server'\nimport { tableSchema } from '@/lib/table-schema'\n\nexport async function POST({ request }: { request: Request }) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, openrouterByok)\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(openrouterByok)\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: createOpenRouterText('openai/gpt-5.5', apiKey),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    threadId: params.threadId,\n    runId: params.runId,\n    outputSchema: tableSchema,\n    stream: true,\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/chat')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST,\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nImport `openrouterByok` from `@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok`, not from the adapter main entry.\n\nRun the app. Paste an OpenRouter key. Send `Compare 6 JavaScript frameworks`. Rows appear as the JSON streams.\n\nThe same app is on the Examples tab at `/ai/latest/docs/framework/react/examples/streaming-structured-table`.\n\n<!-- ::client-example library=ai framework=react slug=streaming-structured-table -->\n\nYou have a table that fills from streamed structured output. The OpenRouter key never sits in a server env file.\n\nThe full example is on GitHub: [TanStack/ai `examples/react/streaming-structured-table`](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/react/streaming-structured-table).\n\nFor the API details, open [Streaming UIs](../structured-outputs/streaming).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Streaming Structured Table\nid: streaming-structured-table\norder: 2\ndescription: \"Stream a typed table from chat({ outputSchema, stream: true }). useChat exposes partial.rows. The UI fills as JSON arrives.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - tutorial\n  - structured output\n  - streaming\n  - useChat\n  - outputSchema\n  - table\n  - openrouter\n  - tanstack start\n---\n\nYou want a table that fills while the model writes JSON. If you wait for the full object, the UI stays empty.\n\nPass `outputSchema` and `stream: true` to `chat()`. Pass the same schema to `useChat`. Show `partial.rows` as table rows.\n\nThis tutorial is React + Start. For other frameworks, open [Quick Start](../getting-started/quick-start).\n\nYou can skip the scaffold and paste a key in the sandbox at the end of this page.\n\nIf you already built [Basic Chat](./basic-chat), keep the key form. Then skip to the schema.\n\n## 1. Create a Start app\n\n```bash\nnpx @tanstack/cli@latest create\n```\n\nPick React. For more options, see [Start getting started](https://tanstack.com/start/latest/docs/framework/react/quick-start).\n\nThen install the TanStack AI packages and Zod:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-react @tanstack/ai-openrouter zod\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nGet an OpenRouter key from [openrouter.ai](https://openrouter.ai).\n\n## Client and server\n\nA structured table has two sides.\n\nThe **client** holds the key, sends the prompt, and shows rows from `partial`.\n\nThe **server** route reads that key, calls OpenRouter with the schema, and streams JSON back.\n\nThe next steps share one schema. Then they save the key. Then they show the table. Then they add the route.\n\n## 2. Share a schema\n\nCreate `src/lib/table-schema.ts`. The client and the server import this file. Field descriptions tell the model what to put in each column.\n\n```typescript\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nexport const tableSchema = z.object({\n  title: z.string().meta({ description: 'Short title for the table' }),\n  rows: z.array(\n    z.object({\n      name: z.string().meta({ description: 'Row name' }),\n      year: z.number().meta({ description: 'First release year' }),\n      kind: z.string().meta({ description: 'Category or paradigm' }),\n      note: z.string().meta({ description: 'One-line typical use' }),\n    }),\n  ),\n})\n```\n\n## 3. Set up BYOK on the client\n\nCreate `src/lib/byok.ts`. `memoryStorage()` keeps the key in this tab.\n\n```typescript\nimport { defineByok, memoryStorage } from '@tanstack/ai-react/byok'\nimport { openrouterByok } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok'\n\nexport const byok = defineByok({\n  storage: memoryStorage(),\n  providers: [openrouterByok],\n})\n```\n\nCreate `src/components/open-router-key-form.tsx`. Export `OpenRouterKeyForm` from that file. If you already have this form from Basic Chat, reuse it.\n\n```tsx ignore\nimport { useState } from 'react'\nimport { openrouterByok } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok'\nimport { useByok } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { byok } from '@/lib/byok'\n\nexport function OpenRouterKeyForm() {\n  const snapshot = useByok(byok)\n  const [draft, setDraft] = useState('')\n  const [error, setError] = useState('')\n  const status = snapshot.status[openrouterByok.id]\n  const masked = status && 'masked' in status ? status.masked : undefined\n  const missingKey = snapshot.prompt?.reason === 'missing'\n\n  return (\n    <form\n      onSubmit={(event) => {\n        event.preventDefault()\n        const next = draft.trim()\n        if (!next) return\n        setError('')\n        void byok\n          .update(openrouterByok.id, next)\n          .then(() => setDraft(''))\n          .catch((caught: unknown) =>\n            setError(\n              caught instanceof Error ? caught.message : 'Could not save key',\n            ),\n          )\n      }}\n    >\n      <input\n        type=\"password\"\n        autoComplete=\"off\"\n        placeholder={masked ? `Saved ${masked}` : 'Paste your OpenRouter key'}\n        value={draft}\n        onChange={(event) => setDraft(event.target.value)}\n      />\n      <button type=\"submit\" disabled={!draft.trim()}>\n        Save key\n      </button>\n      {missingKey ? (\n        <p>Paste an OpenRouter key, then send again.</p>\n      ) : null}\n      {error ? <p>{error}</p> : null}\n    </form>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nIf you want passkeys, open [Bring Your Own Key](../advanced/byok).\n\n## 4. Show the table from `partial`\n\nOpen `src/routes/index.tsx`. Import `OpenRouterKeyForm` from `@/components/open-router-key-form`. Pass `byok` and `outputSchema: tableSchema` to `useChat`.\n\nThe server streams JSON text in chunks. The hook parses that incomplete JSON into `partial`. Fields show up as soon as they parse. A new row can have empty cells until more text arrives.\n\n`final` is the completed object. It stays `null` until the stream ends. If you only read `final`, the table stays empty until the run is done.\n\nShow `partial.rows` while the model writes. Use `final` when you need the complete object, for example to save it.\n\nMissing cells show `…` until that field arrives.\n\n```tsx ignore\nimport { useState } from 'react'\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents, useChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { OpenRouterKeyForm } from '@/components/open-router-key-form'\nimport { byok } from '@/lib/byok'\nimport { tableSchema } from '@/lib/table-schema'\n\nfunction TablePage() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState('')\n  const { sendMessage, isLoading, error, stop, partial, final } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    byok,\n    outputSchema: tableSchema,\n  })\n\n  const rows = partial.rows ?? []\n  const title = partial.title\n\n  const handleSendMessage = () => {\n    if (!input.trim()) return\n    sendMessage(input.trim())\n    setInput('')\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>Streaming structured table</h1>\n      <OpenRouterKeyForm />\n      {rows.length === 0 && !isLoading ? (\n        <p>Paste an OpenRouter key. Then ask for a comparison table.</p>\n      ) : (\n        <table aria-busy={isLoading}>\n          <caption>\n            {title ?? 'Results'}\n            {isLoading ? ' (streaming)' : final ? ' (complete)' : ''}\n          </caption>\n          <thead>\n            <tr>\n              <th scope=\"col\">Name</th>\n              <th scope=\"col\">Year</th>\n              <th scope=\"col\">Kind</th>\n              <th scope=\"col\">Note</th>\n            </tr>\n          </thead>\n          <tbody>\n            {rows.map((row, index) => (\n              <tr key={index}>\n                <th scope=\"row\">{row.name ?? '…'}</th>\n                <td>{row.year ?? '…'}</td>\n                <td>{row.kind ?? '…'}</td>\n                <td>{row.note ?? '…'}</td>\n              </tr>\n            ))}\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n      )}\n      {error ? <p>{error.message}</p> : null}\n      {isLoading ? (\n        <button type=\"button\" onClick={stop}>\n          Stop\n        </button>\n      ) : null}\n      <label htmlFor=\"table-prompt\">Prompt</label>\n      <textarea\n        id=\"table-prompt\"\n        value={input}\n        onChange={(event) => setInput(event.target.value)}\n        placeholder=\"Compare 6 JavaScript frameworks\"\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      />\n      <button\n        type=\"button\"\n        onClick={handleSendMessage}\n        disabled={!input.trim() || isLoading}\n      >\n        Send\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/')({\n  component: TablePage,\n})\n```\n\nA send with no key does not POST. The form shows \"Paste an OpenRouter key, then send again.\"\n\n## 5. Add the server route\n\nCreate `src/routes/api.chat.ts` in the `src/routes` folder, next to `index.tsx`. Start maps that file name to the `/api/chat` path.\n\n`getByokKey` reads the `x-byok-openrouter` header, then `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` in the environment. If both are empty, `byokMissing` returns HTTP 401.\n\nPass `outputSchema: tableSchema` and `stream: true`. Wrap `chat()` with `toServerSentEventsResponse`.\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createOpenRouterText } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter'\nimport { openrouterByok } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok'\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from '@tanstack/ai/byok/server'\nimport { tableSchema } from '@/lib/table-schema'\n\nexport async function POST({ request }: { request: Request }) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, openrouterByok)\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(openrouterByok)\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: createOpenRouterText('openai/gpt-5.5', apiKey),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    threadId: params.threadId,\n    runId: params.runId,\n    outputSchema: tableSchema,\n    stream: true,\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/chat')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST,\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nImport `openrouterByok` from `@tanstack/ai-openrouter/byok`, not from the adapter main entry.\n\nRun the app. Paste an OpenRouter key. Send `Compare 6 JavaScript frameworks`. Rows appear as the JSON streams.\n\nThe same app is on the Examples tab at `/ai/latest/docs/framework/react/examples/streaming-structured-table`.\n\n<!-- ::client-example library=ai framework=react slug=streaming-structured-table -->\n\nYou have a table that fills from streamed structured output. The OpenRouter key never sits in a server env file.\n\nThe full example is on GitHub: [TanStack/ai `examples/react/streaming-structured-table`](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/react/streaming-structured-table).\n\nFor the API details, open [Streaming UIs](../structured-outputs/streaming).\n"}
